<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Augustus Bowles</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1763–1805</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Augustus Bowles was a Maryland-born Loyalist adventurer who married into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Muscogee</a> Confederacy. After escaping Spanish captivity he returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> in 1799 and proclaimed the State of Muskogee, which challenged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> for four years until he was betrayed to the Spanish in 1803 and died a prisoner in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havana">Havana</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-augustus-bowles.jpg" alt="William Augustus Bowles" width="320" height="381" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Bush Hardy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thomas_Hardy_(1757-1804)_-_William_Augustus_Bowles_(1763%E2%80%931805),_as_a_Native_North_American_(Creek)_Chief_-_446698_-_National_Trust.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
